  "id": "COMPOUND:29645 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "Caryptoside is shown to have a target relationship with JM1 through multiple independent pathways, with the core mechanism involving the interaction with MIP, a target of several compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of JM1, suggesting a shared biological role in the pathophysiology of the disease. The presence of multiple distinct targets (MIP, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide) indicates that Caryptoside may act through a common or complementary mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of signaling pathways or enzymatic activities that ultimately influence JM1. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Caryptoside and JM1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
